Translation patch: libsignal_core::curve::PublicKey::deserialize

Change: the `log::warn!` call for trailing bytes moves into the new function `log_public_key_trailing_bytes` at the end of the file, marked `#[track_caller]`. It is called on the line of the old call, with `tail.len()`; a comment takes the other three lines of the old call, so no other line of the file moves.
Why: Aeneas stops with an internal error on `log!` expansions ("Internal error: please file an issue" at the expansion, then `Not_found` in `llbc/FunsAnalysis.ml`). The helper is opaque in the extraction (`aeneas-config.core.yml`).
Behaviour: same log record: level, target, module path, file, line and message. `log` takes the record's location from `Location::caller()` in its `#[track_caller]` function `loc()`; because the helper is `#[track_caller]` too, that location is the helper's call site, the line of the old call. `tail.len()` is computed before the call instead of only when the level is enabled (it has no effect).

diff --git a/rust/core/src/curve.rs b/rust/core/src/curve.rs
--- a/rust/core/src/curve.rs
+++ b/rust/core/src/curve.rs
@@ -92,10 +92,10 @@
                 // We currently allow trailing data after the public key.
                 // TODO: once this is known to not be seen in practice, make this a hard error.
                 if !tail.is_empty() {
-                    log::warn!(
-                        "ECPublicKey deserialized with {} trailing bytes",
-                        tail.len()
-                    );
+                    log_public_key_trailing_bytes(tail.len());
+                    // Modified for Aeneas: the `log!` expansion moves into the helper at the
+                    // end of this file, which the extraction treats as an opaque effect. The
+                    // helper reports this line as the record's location (`#[track_caller]`).
                 }
                 Ok(PublicKey {
                     key: PublicKeyData::DjbPublicKey(*key),
@@ -560,3 +560,10 @@
         );
     }
 }
+
+// Logging helper: Aeneas fails on `log!` expansions, so the extraction treats
+// it as an opaque effect. Level, message and the recorded line are unchanged.
+#[track_caller]
+fn log_public_key_trailing_bytes(trailing: usize) {
+    log::warn!("ECPublicKey deserialized with {} trailing bytes", trailing);
+}
